<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vieille Montagne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vieille Montagne, in German Altenberg, was a zinc ore mine at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kelmis">Kelmis</a> (La Calamine), between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a> and Liège, worked since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> for calamine used in brass-making. In 1816 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> could not agree who should have it and left the surrounding area as Neutral Moresnet. From 1837 the Vieille Montagne company made it a major zinc producer until the ore ran out in the 1880s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vieille-montagne.jpg" alt="Vieille Montagne" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: user:xofc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:080911_wikipedia_0036.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
